/* 
    static/ — Publicly served assets (CSS, JS, images).

    Flask serves everything in this folder at the URL /static/...
    For example, static/style.css is available at /static/style.css.

    In HTML templates, use:
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ url_for('static', filename='style.css') }}">
    
    url_for() is preferred over hard-coding because it works even
    if you later mount the app under a URL prefix (e.g., /myapp/static/).

    This file is a placeholder so Git tracks the empty directory.
*/
